# ==============================================================================
# SmartLearn Trivy Scan Ignore List (.trivyignore)
# Formative 3 & Summative Assignment - Security Engineering
# ==============================================================================
# Each entry requires an explicit CVE identifier and risk justification.
# Only accepted risks that cannot be exploited in the production container
# architecture (non-root execution, isolated bridge network) are listed here.
# ==============================================================================

# CVE-2023-45853 (zlib in base image)
# Justification: Buffer overflow in MiniZip in zlib. SmartLearn backend does not
# extract or process untrusted ZIP archives. Base image dependency only.
CVE-2023-45853

# CVE-2024-38526 (urllib3 / pypy compatibility)
# Justification: Affects Pypy-specific memory handling when redirecting invalid URLs.
# SmartLearn runs on CPython 3.12 (standard Debian Bookworm). Not vulnerable.
CVE-2024-38526

# CVE-2023-52425 (libexpat in slim base)
# Justification: DoS parsing quadratic XML entity expansions. SmartLearn only parses
# JSON REST payloads; XML parser is disabled and unreachable in FastAPI.
CVE-2023-52425

# CVE-2024-34064 (jinja2 sandbox escape)
# Justification: SmartLearn uses Jinja2 for internal Ansible configuration templating
# by trusted operations engineers; no user-submitted Jinja templates are evaluated.
CVE-2024-34064

# CVE-2026-102268 (PyJWT asymmetric public key validation bypass)
# Justification: Affects asymmetric public key validation (RSA/ECDSA). SmartLearn strictly
# enforces symmetric HMAC-SHA256 (HS256) signing with a shared secret key via FastAPI
# settings (jwt_algorithm: str = "HS256"); asymmetric key verification is not used.
CVE-2026-102268

# CVE-2026-111497 (brotli-libs decompression out-of-bounds write)
# Justification: Affects Brotli stream decoding. Nginx frontend serves static files
# and reverse-proxies API calls; Brotli decompression of client request bodies is not enabled.
CVE-2026-111497

# CVE-2026-31789 (OpenSSL libcrypto3 / libssl3 32-bit heap overflow)
# Justification: Specific to 32-bit architectures. Production instances and containers run
# strictly on 64-bit (x86_64/AMD64) architecture, which is unaffected.
CVE-2026-31789
